+### `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology`
+
+- Exact claim: for $0\le r\le3$ and every finite-rank holomorphic vector bundle $E$ on $\mathbb P^r$, the analytic sheaf cohomology is canonically the cohomology of the global smooth $E$-valued Dolbeault complex; for $E=\mathcal O$, $H^0=\mathbb C$ and all positive cohomology vanishes.
+- Conventions/proof route: define $\bar\partial_E$ coefficientwise in holomorphic frames and verify it is frame-independent; resolve $\mathcal O(E)$ by smooth $E$-valued $(0,q)$-forms; use the local polydisc lemma, CR characterization, smooth-module acyclicity, full AC implies DC, and the supplied acyclic-resolution theorem. The scalar values use the preceding Laurent/Čech lemma. No metric, Hodge, GAGA, or arbitrary coherent-sheaf vanishing premise is used.
+- Dependencies: local projective/vector-bundle/twisting definitions, bigraded forms, sheaf cohomology, local Dolbeault and CR suppliers, smooth-module acyclicity, acyclic-resolution theorem, AC⇒DC, and the local Laurent/Čech lemma; all are declared mathematical premises. Computed item level 2.
+- Sources/locators: Lebl §4.4 pp. 142–145; MIT 18.117 lectures 4 and 7–9 (PDF pp. 9–12, 18–23); Dervan–Kuang §§3.1–3.2 and 4.4–4.5; Serre §13 retained only as historical context.
