+## Item checkpoints
+
+### `def-qftx-gaga-projective-twisting-line-bundles`
+
+- Exact claim: for each $r\ge1$, define the standard holomorphic line bundles $\mathcal O(k)$ on $\mathbb P^r(\mathbb C)$ by their homogeneous-coordinate transition functions; $\mathcal O(0)$ is the structure sheaf.
+- Conventions: chart $U_i={Z_i\ne0}$; $\mathcal O(k)$ uses transitions $ e_j=(Z_j/Z_i)^k e_i$. The cocycle identity is checked directly in the definition.
+- Dependencies: `def-complex-projective-space-and-holomorphic-charts`, `def-complex-manifolds-and-holomorphic-vector-bundles`; both are exact imported mathematical definitions, and their homes are already required by the current plan.
+- Decision: authored as the first A-page carrier at item dependency level 0.
+- Result/checks: the Definition explicitly verifies the transition factors are holomorphic and nowhere zero and satisfy the identity, inverse and triple-overlap cocycle equations. MIT 18.117 lecture 7 and Cambridge *Complex Manifolds* §5 are the two inspected independent treatments; the actual cocycle check is local. It is in the A-page inventory at level 0, and the author, content, rendering, dependency, proof-layout, contract, and readiness checks pass.
+- Unresolved obligations: none within this item. Later independent review/approval remains part of the native workflow.
+
+### `lem-qftx-gaga-projective-cover-laurent-cohomology`
+
+- Planned claim: projective-standard-cover analytic Čech computation for $\mathcal O$, $\mathcal O(-1)$, and $\mathcal O(-r-1)$ for $0\le r\le3$, including acyclic intersections and normally convergent coefficient homotopies.
+- Conventions: standard homogeneous coordinates; $\mathcal O(k)$ sections are degree-$k$ homogeneous holomorphic data; increasing-index Čech differential has alternating restriction signs; AC is explicit.
+- Dependencies: `def-qftx-gaga-projective-twisting-line-bundles`, the 11 used suppliers among the 12 inspected planned suppliers, the exact Hartogs/pseudoconvexity definitions above, and the derived-global-sections definition. The planned slice-coefficient lemma is rejected for this use by its actual Hartogs-figure hypothesis; the alternative iterated-Cauchy argument is proved in the item. All used edges are mathematical premises; no physical assumptions.
+- Source disposition: Lebl gives the analytic methods, but his multivariable Laurent expansion is only an exercise; MIT and Cambridge provide independent projective/Čech context with proof-scope limits; Serre is retained as a non-proof historical note.
+- Decision: authored as the second A-page carrier at item dependency level 1. It uses the exact local twisting-bundle definition and the inspected imported interfaces, including full AC/DC strength, local Dolbeault exactness, the smooth-module acyclicity theorem, the derived-functor comparison, iterated Cauchy/Laurent coefficients, pseudoconvex scalar solvability, and Leray/Čech comparison.
+- Exact claim/conventions: for $r\le3$, the standard-cover intersections are $\mathbb C^a\times(\mathbb C^*)^b$; their equal-radius boundary radius is the minimum modulus in punctured coordinates, so $-\log\delta$ is the finite maximum of harmonic coordinate functions. Each $\mathcal O(k)$ section has unique normally convergent modes of total degree $k$, with negative support contained in the cover index. Proper nonempty negative support contracts with the increasing-index sign; the zero and full-support boundary modes yield the listed scalar and negative-twist groups.
+- Sources/locators: Lebl v4.4 §§1.1–1.2, 2.5, 4.4 (printed pp. 15–23, 90–101, 142–145); MIT 18.117 lectures 7–9, 11 (PDF pp. 18–25); Dervan–Kuang §§3.1–3.2, 4.4–4.5 (printed pp. 9–11, 23–26); Serre §13 Lemma 4 / footnote 4 (pp. 20–21, context only). Each exercise or outline is explicitly identified as incomplete and completed locally.
+- Result/checks: the full conditional proof, intersection acyclicity, mode decomposition, sign contraction, normal convergence, and point case are authored. The exact mixed-parameter argument uses fixed iterated contour order and termwise integration justified by a uniform bound. The normative precheck's dependency-layer repair changed only phase.step labels and backward step references; the contract was regenerated from the resulting proof. Manifest, proof-layout, strict-contract, citation-fidelity, source, author, dependency-level and individual readiness checks pass.
+- Unresolved obligations: none mathematical at the inspected interfaces. The run-wide readiness check is held by the out-of-batch YAML defect recorded in the final section.
+
+### `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-dolbeault-scalar-cohomology`
+
+- Exact claim: for $0\le r\le3$ and every finite-rank holomorphic vector bundle $E$ on $\mathbb P^r$, the analytic sheaf cohomology is canonically the cohomology of the global smooth $E$-valued Dolbeault complex; for $E=\mathcal O$, $H^0=\mathbb C$ and all positive cohomology vanishes.
+- Conventions/proof route: define $\bar\partial_E$ coefficientwise in holomorphic frames and verify it is frame-independent; resolve $\mathcal O(E)$ by smooth $E$-valued $(0,q)$-forms; use the local polydisc lemma, CR characterization, smooth-module acyclicity, full AC implies DC, and the supplied acyclic-resolution theorem. The scalar values use the preceding Laurent/Čech lemma. No metric, Hodge, GAGA, or arbitrary coherent-sheaf vanishing premise is used.
+- Dependencies: local projective/vector-bundle/twisting definitions, bigraded forms, sheaf cohomology, local Dolbeault and CR suppliers, smooth-module acyclicity, acyclic-resolution theorem, AC⇒DC, and the local Laurent/Čech lemma; all are declared mathematical premises. Computed item level 2.
+- Sources/locators: Lebl §4.4 pp. 142–145; MIT 18.117 lectures 4 and 7–9 (PDF pp. 9–12, 18–23); Dervan–Kuang §§3.1–3.2 and 4.4–4.5; Serre §13 retained only as historical context.
+- Result/checks: complete conditional proof and the $r=0$ point case are authored. The proof contract and all scoped authoring checks pass; its item level is 2 and its current readiness record is closed.
+
+### `ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-projective-structure`
+
+- Exact claim: on $\mathbb P^2$, the degree-zero mode is the only empty-negative-support mode, every other mode has proper nonempty support and contracts, and the scalar analytic and global Dolbeault cohomology are $\mathbb C$ in degree zero and zero above.
+- Conventions/dependencies: three charts ordered $0<1<2$; increasing-index Čech differential; local mode supplier and general projective Dolbeault theorem. The proof writes the finite $C^0\to C^1\to C^2$ matrices and checks kernel, image and surjectivity.
+- Sources/locators: Lebl §§1.2, 4.4; MIT lectures 7–9, 11; Cambridge §4; Serre §13 is non-proof historical context.
+- Result/checks: complete three-chart contraction, explicit zero-mode matrices and local-uniform-convergence argument authored; its contract and scoped checks pass, and its level-3 readiness record is closed.
+
+### `ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-untwisted-obstruction`
+
+- Exact claim: for $1\le r\le3$, the degree-weighted Laurent modes give $H^0(\mathcal O(-1))=0$ and exactly one surviving top mode for $\mathcal O(-r-1)$, so the latter top group is $\mathbb C$; the nonzero line-bundle fibers then show $\mathcal O(-1)$ is not globally generated. The theorem comparison supplies the corresponding global Dolbeault groups.
+- Conventions/dependencies: total homogeneous degree $k$, negative support $N(m)$, top support $\{0,\ldots,r\}$; uses the local Laurent/Čech supplier and the general Dolbeault theorem. No GAGA or algebraic cohomology is invoked.
+- Sources/locators: Lebl §1.2; MIT lectures 7–9, 11; Cambridge §§4–5; Serre §13 is non-proof context only.
+- Result/checks: complete degree constraints, top-boundary quotient, unique mode, and fiber evaluation argument authored; its contract and scoped checks pass, and its level-3 readiness record is closed.
